   "reasoning_summary": "C10H10O has DoU 6, consistent with a phenyl ring, a C=C and a C=O. The 13C carbonyl at 198.2 (7) indicates a conjugated methyl ketone, and the CH3 at 2.32/27.3 (6,14) is an acetyl group. Signals at 143.2 (8) and 127.0 (13) are the beta and alpha enone CH carbons. The vinyl proton at 6.68 (5) is the alpha H; the beta H overlaps the aromatic signals at 7.46-7.49. A monosubstituted phenyl accounts for 134.2, 130.3, 128.8 and 128.1 (9-12). All shifts match literature values for (E)-benzylideneacetone. The alternative isomers fail on the carbonyl shift or the methyl shift and multiplicity."
  },
